# Gui's Photos

Static photography portfolio for Gui Roque.

The site is intentionally simple: plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript with a small build script that turns image files into gallery data. There is no CMS and no runtime API.

## Open Locally

Open `index.html` in a browser.

The site does not depend on runtime `fetch()` calls, so it works from a normal file open and from static hosting like GitHub Pages.

## Add Photos

1. Drop gallery images into `assets/images/`.
2. Commit and push to `main`.
3. GitHub Pages runs `npm run generate:gallery` during deployment.
4. New images are added to the top of the gallery automatically.

For local previews after adding images:

```bash
npm run generate:gallery
```

Do not edit `data/gallery.js` by hand. It is generated from `assets/images/` and `data/gallery-meta.json`.

If you add `assets/images/about-portrait.jpg` later, the generator will skip it so it can be used on the about page instead of the gallery.

## Optional Image Metadata

Use `data/gallery-meta.json` when an image needs extra detail, such as:

- `alt`
- `cameraSettings`
- `imageResolution`

The image detail page only shows camera shot info when `cameraSettings` or `imageResolution` is present.

## Project Structure

- `index.html` - homepage and gallery grid.
- `views/about.html` - about page.
- `views/faq.html` - FAQ page.
- `views/work.html` - selected work detail page.
- `styles/global.css` - shared design system, layout, responsive rules, and animations.
- `components/site-header.js` - shared header, navigation, social links, and image fade setup.
- `components/work-grid.js` - homepage gallery rendering.
- `components/work-detail.js` - selected work rendering and optional camera details.
- `components/faq-list.js` - FAQ categories and accordion behavior.
- `data/faq.js` - FAQ content.
- `data/gallery-meta.json` - optional metadata for gallery images.
- `data/gallery.js` - generated gallery data; do not edit manually.
- `scripts/build-gallery-data.js` - scans `assets/images/` and writes `data/gallery.js`.
- `assets/images/` - gallery images.
- `assets/icons/` - social icons.
- `.github/workflows/pages.yml` - regenerates gallery data and deploys the static site on push.
- `CNAME` - custom domain config for GitHub Pages; keep it at the root.

## Deployment

Push to `main`. The Pages workflow builds the gallery data and uploads the static site artifact.
